---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Docs" description="Install, set up and use ghdeck.">
  <section class="hero" style="padding:56px 0 4px">
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,40px)">Docs</h1>
    <p class="lead">Install, connect, use.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="doc">
    <h2 id="install">Install</h2>

    <h3>Homebrew</h3>
    <pre class="block">brew install jitendravjh/tap/ghdeck</pre>
    <p>Upgrade with <code>brew upgrade ghdeck</code>.</p>

    <h3>Download a binary</h3>
    <p>Nothing else needed. <code>uname -m</code> tells you which Mac you have.</p>
    <p class="plat">macOS, Apple Silicon</p>
    <pre class="block">curl -sSfL https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck/releases/latest/download/ghdeck-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz | tar xz
sudo mv ghdeck /usr/local/bin/</pre>
    <p class="plat">macOS, Intel</p>
    <pre class="block">curl -sSfL https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck/releases/latest/download/ghdeck-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz | tar xz
sudo mv ghdeck /usr/local/bin/</pre>
    <p class="plat">Linux, x86_64</p>
    <pre class="block">curl -sSfL https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck/releases/latest/download/ghdeck-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar xz
sudo mv ghdeck /usr/local/bin/</pre>
    <p class="plat">Linux, arm64</p>
    <pre class="block">curl -sSfL https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck/releases/latest/download/ghdeck-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar xz
sudo mv ghdeck /usr/local/bin/</pre>
    <p>Linux builds are static, so any distro works. Checksums are on the <a href="https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck/releases/latest">release</a>. Downloading through a browser rather than curl leaves a macOS quarantine flag, cleared with <code>xattr -d com.apple.quarantine ghdeck</code>.</p>

    <h3>From source</h3>
    <p>Only if you want to build it yourself. Needs Rust 1.88 and a C compiler.</p>
    <pre class="block">cargo install --git https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck ghdeck</pre>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <h2 id="setup">Setup</h2>
    <p>Pick one, then run <code>ghdeck</code>.</p>
    <h3>With gh</h3>
    <pre class="block">gh auth login</pre>
    <h3>With a token</h3>
    <p>Needs the <code>repo</code> scope, from <a href="https://github.com/settings/tokens">github.com/settings/tokens</a>. Put it in your shell profile. gh is not needed this way.</p>
    <pre class="block">export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_here</pre>
    <p>The first run caches everything, a few seconds. After that it opens instantly and refreshes on its own.</p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <h2 id="use">Use</h2>
    <pre class="block">ghdeck                                    <span class="d"># dashboard</span>
ghdeck list                               <span class="d"># what needs attention</span>
ghdeck list all                           <span class="d"># everything</span>
ghdeck show JuliaGeometry/Meshes.jl#1428  <span class="d"># one conversation</span>
ghdeck sync                               <span class="d"># refresh now</span></pre>
    <p>Filters are <code>attention</code>, <code>open</code>, <code>yours</code>, <code>to-review</code> and <code>all</code>. Attention means open items that are conflicting, have changes requested, have CI failing, or wait on your review.</p>

    <h3>Keys</h3>
    <table class="keys">
      <tr><td>up down</td><td>move</td></tr>
      <tr><td>left right</td><td>switch filter</td></tr>
      <tr><td>1 to 5</td><td>jump to a filter</td></tr>
      <tr><td>enter</td><td>read the conversation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>o</td><td>open in browser</td></tr>
      <tr><td>y</td><td>copy url</td></tr>
      <tr><td>r</td><td>sync</td></tr>
      <tr><td>/</td><td>search</td></tr>
      <tr><td>?</td><td>help</td></tr>
      <tr><td>q</td><td>quit</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>In a conversation, up and down scroll, <code>b</code> expands bot messages, left or esc goes back.</p>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
